---
import PhysicsDiagram from "./PhysicsDiagram.astro";

// Pattern study: Rauno's two-column with mono eyebrow row + Linear's
// long-form prose paired with a technical illustration. No buzzwords,
// no future-tense overpromising. Names the prior art (Embr Wave, PMV/
// PPD) so the claim is anchored to existing research, not vibes.
---

<section class="relative">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1280px] px-6 sm:px-10 py-32 sm:py-40">
    <div class="mb-16 flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-grid pb-6">
      <span class="mono-label">01 / the honest part</span>
      <span class="mono-label tabular hidden sm:inline">mechanism · prior art · constraints</span>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[5fr_6fr] gap-14 lg:gap-20 items-start">
      <div class="max-w-[560px]">
        <h2 class="font-sans font-medium text-[34px] sm:text-[44px] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] text-fg">
          The mechanism is real.
          <br />
          <span class="text-fg-muted">The constraints are too.</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-[16px] sm:text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-fg-muted">
          <p>
            The inner wrist places skin within a millimetre of two of the
            body's most accessible arteries: the radial and the ulnar. Heat
            moving through that skin reaches blood quickly, and the brain
            reads the signal as an overall change in thermal comfort, not a
            local one. This is the mechanism behind Embr Wave and the body
            of thermal-comfort research going back to Fanger's PMV/PPD model.
          </p>
          <p>
            Aegis sits on the same principle. A small Peltier element pressed
            against the inner wrist can either pull heat off the skin or push
            heat into it, in short bursts that feel disproportionately
            effective. Peltier modules are not efficient at moving large
            amounts of heat over long periods. They are excellent at
            delivering a few watts of cooling or heating exactly where the
            body is most receptive, for a few minutes at a time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ul class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-fg-muted">
          <li class="flex justify-between border-t border-grid pt-3">
            <span>COP target</span>
            <span class="text-fg tabular">~1.2</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex justify-between border-t border-grid pt-3">
            <span>Burst</span>
            <span class="text-fg tabular">30–180 s</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex justify-between border-t border-grid pt-3">
            <span>Comfort band</span>
            <span class="text-fg tabular">32–34 &#176;c</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex justify-between border-t border-grid pt-3">
            <span>Peak draw</span>
            <span class="text-fg tabular">~4.5 w</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="w-full">
        <PhysicsDiagram />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
